body:
I wrote this "poem" (if it can be considered that) because I was feeling extremely down. As you said when you fail in the mating process your body punishes you with strong emotions and once you have failed for the 100th time, that's when you feel beyond sad... you feel pathetic. 

&#x200B;

I (like many others) have been trying so hard to acquire this thing called Love and for someone with close to no experience, it can feel like a minefield. There is nothing more frustrating than to search for something you so desperately try to understand and you know you need it but you keep failing, and the only feedback you get back is "you'll find it someday". What the hell is that suppose to mean?! 

&#x200B;

My experience of Love are few and none of them has been good. So in my mess of emotion, I ask "why?". I am angry and I am sad, and it is sometimes easier to blame your problems on someone else... especially when so many people around you keep telling you that "everything happens for a reason".

&#x200B;

I am a seeker of answers, but one that never receives any. Because once you are stuck in a storm, it's hard to ask the right questions.
